The Renaissance icon packs (neo-launcher/iconpacks/renaissance-*), generated, one script for all four:

    python3 -I make-renaissance-pack.py ../../neo-launcher/iconpacks/renaissance-day          --style tile   --mode day
    python3 -I make-renaissance-pack.py ../../neo-launcher/iconpacks/renaissance-night        --style tile   --mode night
    python3 -I make-renaissance-pack.py ../../neo-launcher/iconpacks/renaissance-glyph-day    --style glyph  --mode day
    python3 -I make-renaissance-pack.py ../../neo-launcher/iconpacks/renaissance-glyph-night  --style glyph  --mode night

Tile (the launcher's home grid and dock, `de.yesman.neo icon-pack`): full-bleed 256 px squares in the quick-settings
inactive tile's design (extension/qs.js: a flat rounded square, corner radius 24/76 of its width, the fill and the ink
of the look's tiles) with the app's Material glyph centred, flat, no frame and no neon. Day is the day looks' cream
tile with dark ink, night the night looks' dark tile with light ink; Minerva's own icon (`yesman`) is the owl (owl.png,
derived from the Minerva agent image). One pack serves each pair of looks, so the day fill is marble's and sea's shared
cream and the night fill forest's and plum's shared near-black. The launcher paints drawn icons at the full icon size
over nothing (neo-launcher/src/icons.c icons_render), so the tile fills the icon box and pack.json has no shape; `scale`
(0.5) and `iconback` (the tile alone) only serve apps the pack does not draw. gnome-map.json is the same desktop-id map
as the round pack's; appfilter.json is empty.

Glyph (for Neo Settings' rows and search results, not the launcher): only the fine-line glyph and its neon aura on
transparent, in a marble (day) or granite (night) ink. icons/<name>.png for every icon-name string Neo Settings uses
(apps/settings/src, "-symbolic" suffix kept) and the short names of the mock-up (wifi bt display sound notif battery
account lock minerva apps); icons.txt lists them. The colour is the area's.

Glyphs are Material Symbols Outlined, weight 200 (Google, Apache-2.0: glyphs/LICENSE), fetched by fetch-glyphs.sh from
github.com/google/material-design-icons (symbols/web/<name>/materialsymbolsoutlined/<name>_wght200_48px.svg) and
committed. The script needs python3-gi with Rsvg 2.0, python3-cairo and python3-pil. Output is
deterministic (textures are seeded from the icon's name). To add an app: a line in TILED (glyph) and its desktop
id in MAP; to add a Settings icon: a line in GLYPHS; then run fetch-glyphs.sh and the four commands above.
